  "solution": {
    "text": "(i) <strong>Hofmann’s bromamide reaction</strong>: The conversion of a primary amide to a primary amine, containing one carbon atom less than the original amide, on heating with a mixture of &nbsp;<math> <mrow> <msub> <mrow> <mtext>Br</mtext> </mrow> <mn>2</mn> </msub> </mrow> </math> &nbsp;in presence of &nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mtext>NaOH</mtext> </mrow> </math> &nbsp;is called Hofmann’s bromide reaction<br /><br /><math> <mtable columnalign=\"left\"> <mtr> <mtd> <msub> <mtext>CH</mtext> <mtext>3</mtext> </msub> <msub> <mtext>CONH</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo><msub> <mtext>Br</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mtext>NaOH</mtext><mo>→</mo><mtext> </mtext><msub> <mtext>CH</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msub> <mtext> </mtext><msub> <mtext>NH</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mtext>NaBr</mtext><mo>+</mo><msub> <mtext>Na</mtext> <mn>2</mn> </msub> <mtext> </mtext><msub> <mtext>CO</mtext> <mn>3</mn> </msub> <mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><msub> <mtext>H</mtext> <mtext>2</mtext> </msub> <mtext>​</mtext><mtext>O</mtext> </mtd> </mtr> <mtr> <mtd> <math display='block'> <mrow>  <mtext>Acetamide</mtext></mrow></math><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mtext> </mtext><mi>Methylamine</mi> </mtd> </mtr> </mtable> </math><br /><br />(ii) <strong>Gabriel phthalimide reaction:</strong> This is a very convenient method for the preparation of pure aliphatic and aryl primary amines.<br /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/77141.png\" style=\"width: 282px; height: 171px;\" /><br /><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/nta_abhyas/jee_main/images/7714.PNG\" style=\"width: 250px; height: 191px;\" /><p>&nbsp;</p>",
